From aa146da57e5149d5452bf490d6a1ac9f8454b442 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vop3p <69450118+Vop3p@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:39:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] ggml-cuda: Q8_K style MMQ activations for K-quants on the
 dp4a path (opt-in GGML_CUDA_MMQ_Q8K)

New activation layout MMQ_Q8_1_DS_LAYOUT_DK for Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K: 1 fp32 scale per
128 values (GGML_CUDA_MMQ_Q8K_BLOCK) + int16 sums of the quantized values per 32
values. The sub-block scales and mins are applied as 24-bit integer multiplies
over the 64 values of one impl call, then 1 float conversion.

E376 on gfx1030: test-backend-ops MUL_MAT 1304/1304; q5_K 25.9 -> 28.2 TFLOPS,
q6_K 25.3 -> 27.6, q4_K 25.9 -> 27.8; Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q5_K_XL prefill +3.5-4.5%;
KLD 0.003941 -> 0.003736 (256 values per scale: 0.004917, rejected).

WIP: dp4a path only, the mma paths do not read this layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
